{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le06ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le06ob11re2img13.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le06ob11re2img13.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: <br>Vanessa! While I was walking through the streets of Jerusalem, I saw a gorgeous, rainbow-colored, stained glass window. It was bigger and brighter than others around. I was looking at it when I realized the two people in the image looked like you and Marco. I read it was Saint Marco and his love! It was the strangest thing!", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le06ob11re2img13.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:<br>Sally! When I read your email, I was hanging out with Marco! I was shocked to hear about the window! Marco is still the nicest guy. We are spending a lot of time together.", "id": 2, "time": "22000", "image": "engenn5le06ob11re2img14.jpg"}, {"text": "In fact, I'm getting ready right now to go out for dinner. He's taking me to this romantic, little, Italian cafe. I think he has something up his sleeve ... he can be very mysterious. I think I'm falling for him ...", "id": 3, "time": "35500", "image": "engenn5le06ob11re2img14.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa Makes a New Friend"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Falling for Marco "}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le06ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Past Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about something that was happening at a particular time in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is how you form the Past Continuous tense:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "subject + was/were + verb-ing<br> I was cooking. <br>It was raining."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often use the Past Continuous tense together with the Simple Past tense.<br> The Past Continuous talks about a longer \u2018background' action. <br>The Simple Past talks about a shorter event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the words <span class=\"strong\">when</span> and <span class=\"strong\">while</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the timeline:"}, {"type": "image", "content": "engenn5le06ob11img01.jpg"}, {"type": "example", "content": "While I was walking in Jerusalem, I saw a beautiful window!"}, {"type": "example", "content": " When I read your email, I was hanging out with Marco."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gorgeous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very beautiful "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The new sous chef is gorgeous!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Comparative and Superlative Adjectives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use a comparative to compare somebody or something to <span class=\"strong\">one </span>other person or thing. <br>You use a superlative to compare somebody or something to the whole <span class=\"strong\">group</span> that he, she or it belongs to."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The window was bigger and brighter than others around. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for information on how to form the comparative and superlative:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Comparative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Superlative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tall\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"taller (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the tallest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Most adjectives: +er, +-est\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"late\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"later (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the latest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives ending in -e: +r, +-st\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happier (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the happiest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2-syllable adjectives ending in -y: +ier, +iest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"attractive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more attractive (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the most attractive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"3+-syllable adjectives: <br><br> more + adjective+ than<br><br>  most + adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"good<br>bad\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"better (than) <br> worse (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the best<br>the worst\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Irregular comparisons\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li> You use <span class=\"strong\">than</span> after comparatives.</li><li>  You add <span class=\"strong\">the</span> in front of the superlative form to describe people, places and things.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was the strangest thing!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "strange"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "odd; unusual "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Everyone I meet is really strange!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mysterious "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "difficult to understand or know "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I like my men mysterious and quiet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hang out "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to spend time with someone "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm hanging out with Marco."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rainbow"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "different colors in the sky caused by light going through water "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A rainbow appeared in the sky."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cut a piece of paper in 8 pieces. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "On each piece, write a verb in the Present tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Flip the papers over and choose two at random."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a Past Continuous sentence using <span class=\"italic\">when</span> or <span class=\"italic\">while</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Try to make funny sentences. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the sentences to your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write 8 action words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make funny sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read the sentences to my partner."}]}], "type": "sena"}